1. Product positioning and non-goals

1.1 Target user

One independent software engineer based in India, with a verified profile initially describing 4 years of MERN/full-stack experience and strengths in React, Next.js, TypeScript, Node.js, NestJS, Express, MongoDB, PostgreSQL and GraphQL.

These are initial seed values from prior profile context, not immutable truths. The user must be able to edit and confirm every profile fact, availability, rate, capacity, portfolio entry and location preference.

1.2 Product promise

“Find the best legitimate opportunities for my actual capabilities, explain why they fit, prepare an evidence-backed application, and keep me in control.”

1.3 Explicit non-goals for MVP

• No automatic bidding, proposal submission, messaging, or account actions.
• No CAPTCHA solving, stealth browser automation, session-cookie harvesting, or bot-detection bypass.
• No scraping a marketplace unless its current terms and technical rules explicitly permit the intended use.
• No claim that an API is available just because a platform has a developer portal.
• No multi-tenant SaaS, billing, team workspaces, Kubernetes or microservices.
• No mandatory paid LLM.
• No fabricated client trust metrics, salary, budget, project history, user achievements or outcomes.
• No automatic inference that a listing is open merely because its URL returns HTTP 200.

