5. User profile and Portfolio Intelligence

5.1 Verified profile

Store:

• Name and headline.
• Years of experience (user-confirmed).
• Skills with proficiency and evidence.
• Preferred project types.
• Preferred geography/timezone.
• Availability and weekly capacity.
• Minimum acceptable hourly/fixed budget.
• Preferred currencies.
• Communication preferences.
• Languages.
• Profile summary.
• Resume versions (only if user chooses to upload).

All rate/availability fields are preferences that can change, not immutable claims.

5.2 Portfolio evidence library — P0, not a later nice-to-have

Each portfolio entry:

• Project name and industry.
• Product category.
• Project context/problem.
• User’s exact role and contribution.
• Technologies actually used.
• Architecture and important decisions.
• Features delivered.
• Outcomes/metrics only when evidence exists.
• Public demo/repository/case-study URL.
• Screenshot/file references.
• Confidentiality flag.
• Evidence verification status.
• Last reviewed date.

Do not infer the user’s role or results from a project title. User must confirm every claim.

5.3 Evidence-to-opportunity matching

For each opportunity, select up to 3 relevant portfolio examples and explain:

• which requirements each example supports;
• which technologies overlap;
• what experience is transferable;
• what is not evidenced and must not be claimed.

A proposal fact should be traceable to either:

• verified profile field;
• verified portfolio evidence;
• opportunity text;
• user-approved custom statement.

