6. Opportunity Intelligence Engine

The system should produce an analysis record, not just a score.

6.1 Analysis dimensions

• Project type and deliverables.
• Required vs optional skills.
• Scope and complexity.
• Budget/rate and currency.
• Estimated effort range (with uncertainty).
• Deadline and urgency.
• Client/platform credibility signals.
• Competition signals, only if source provides reliable data.
• Location/timezone eligibility.
• Red flags and missing information.
• Questions to ask the client.
• Relevant portfolio evidence.
• Recommended next action.

6.2 Client credibility: evidence, not fake ratings

Store provider-supplied fields separately from inferred signals.

• Rating, review count, spend, payment verification: null unless source explicitly provides them.
• Platform identity/verification badges: record source and timestamp.
• External domain/business checks: only use lawful public data; show evidence and confidence.
• No “verified client” label based on a company logo or domain alone.
• A platform’s own verification badge is not a guarantee of payment or project legitimacy.

6.3 Competition analysis

Do not promise competitor/bid-count analysis unless source API supplies it and terms permit it.

If unavailable:

• mark competition UNKNOWN;
• optionally show qualitative indicators such as listing age or source-provided proposal count;
• never manufacture a “low competition” score.

