7. Matching and ranking model

7.1 Two scoring profiles

Freelance Project score — 100 points

|Dimension                     |Weight|Evidence                                                       |
|------------------------------|-----:|---------------------------------------------------------------|
|Technical fit                 |20    |Required/optional skills and stack                             |
|Portfolio evidence fit        |20    |Verified projects mapped to requirements                       |
|Budget/economic fit           |15    |Actual budget/rate, currency, estimated effort                 |
|Client/platform evidence      |15    |Only provider-supplied, attributable signals                   |
|Scope clarity and feasibility |10    |Deliverables, acceptance criteria, deadline                    |
|Competition/opportunity timing|10    |Source-provided bid count/age only; otherwise unknown          |
|Location/timezone fit         |5     |Eligibility and working hours                                  |
|Risk indicators               |5     |Suspicious payment requests, vague scope, off-platform pressure|

Remote Role score — 100 points

|Dimension                    |Weight|
|-----------------------------|-----:|
|Technical fit                |25    |
|Portfolio/experience evidence|15    |
|Compensation fit             |15    |
|India/timezone eligibility   |15    |
|Employment-type preference   |10    |
|Seniority fit                |10    |
|Freshness/status confidence  |5     |
|Employer/listing risk        |5     |

7.2 Scoring rules

• Score only known inputs; missing fields do not silently receive positive values.
• Show coverage/confidence separately from score.
• Do not equate “unknown client rating” with “bad client”; show unknown evidence and reduce confidence.
• Hard disqualifiers (not eligible in India, closed, requires payment to apply, clearly unrelated) should be filters, not just small score penalties.
• Currency conversion must store source amount, currency, timestamp and FX source; never compare USD and INR as if equal.
• Fixed-price feasibility must account for estimated effort and effective hourly return.
• Skill matching must use normalized taxonomy/synonyms, not substring matching that creates false positives.
• User feedback should tune preferences, but never silently rewrite verified profile facts.

7.3 Explainability UI

Show:

• Match score.
• Confidence: high/medium/low.
• Why it matches.
• Missing evidence.
• Risks.
• Estimated effort and budget confidence.
• Recommended action.

