11. Data model and lifecycle

Design schema from workflows, not from an arbitrary list of entities.

Core entities:

• User (single owner in MVP; retain ownership field for future isolation).
• FreelancerProfile.
• Skill and ProfileSkill (or normalized skill JSON initially).
• PortfolioProject and PortfolioEvidence.
• SourceRegistry.
• SourceCredential (encrypted, optional, provider-specific).
• DiscoveryRun.
• Opportunity.
• OpportunitySourceReference (allows the same canonical opportunity to be observed from multiple sources).
• OpportunitySnapshot.
• OpportunityVerification.
• OpportunityAnalysis.
• MatchEvaluation.
• Proposal and ProposalVersion.
• Application.
• ApplicationEvent.
• UserFeedback.
• AuditEvent.

Opportunity key strategy:

1. (sourceId, externalId) where stable provider ID exists.
2. Canonical URL unique per source.
3. Cross-source fingerprint as a candidate duplicate, not automatic merge unless confidence is high.
4. Preserve every source reference and original link.

Important fields:

• opportunityType: FREELANCE_PROJECT / CONTRACT_ROLE / FULL_TIME_ROLE / PART_TIME_ROLE / UNKNOWN.
• sourceStatus: provider’s raw status.
• availabilityStatus: OPEN / CLOSED / UNKNOWN / NEEDS_RECHECK.
• clientRating, reviewCount, spend, paymentVerified: nullable.
• budgetMin, budgetMax, hourlyMin, hourlyMax: nullable with currency and period.
• firstSeenAt, lastSeenAt, lastVerifiedAt, postedAt, expiresAt.
• sourcePayloadHash, not unlimited raw payload retention.
• classificationConfidence, analysisConfidence.

