12. Security, privacy and compliance

• Owner-only authentication for every private route.
• Secure HttpOnly/SameSite cookies, CSRF protection, login rate limits.
• Strict CORS allowlist.
• DTO/schema validation.
• Encrypted OAuth/API tokens at rest.
• Secrets only in deployment secret manager.
• Audit changes, approvals, integration connect/disconnect.
• Least-privilege database access.
• No marketplace passwords stored.
• Clear delete/disconnect workflow.
• Do not retain raw resume or email data unless required and user-consented.

SSRF controls for manual URL intake

• Accept only http/https, preferably https.
• Restrict automatic fetch to known allowed domains.
• Reject localhost, loopback, private, link-local, multicast and reserved IP ranges.
• Resolve DNS and validate every resolved address; defend against DNS rebinding.
• Disable redirects or revalidate every redirect destination.
• Limit timeout, response size, content type and ports.
• Never fetch arbitrary URLs from privileged internal network.
• For MVP, safest path is user-pasted text/metadata plus opening the original URL in the user’s browser.

Platform compliance rules

• Official API or permission only.
• Preserve attribution and original application URLs.
• Respect quotas, cache instructions, deletion/expiry rules and robots/terms where relevant.
• Do not evade access controls.
• Do not store cookies or passwords to imitate user sessions.
• Record source terms URL, reviewed date and permitted use in SourceRegistry.

