13. Cloud execution and reliability

The PC must not be required to run scheduled discovery.

Recommended MVP:

• Railway web service.
• Railway API service.
• One Railway worker/scheduler process.
• Managed PostgreSQL.
• Redis only if queue/locking needs justify it.

Reliability requirements:

• Durable DiscoveryRun records.
• Idempotent upserts.
• Single-run lock per provider/schedule.
• Retry with exponential backoff and jitter.
• Respect Retry-After.
• Provider circuit breaker and health status.
• Worker heartbeat and missed-run alert.
• Never interpret provider outage as an empty feed.
• Database-backed queue or durable job state for important tasks.
• Graceful shutdown and retry-safe jobs.

Suggested schedules:

• Himalayas: once daily (data refresh is daily).
• Jobicy: 2–4 times daily, respecting minimum interval and current docs.
• Remote OK: 2–4 times daily subject to current fair use.
• Marketplace sources: only documented quota and access permit; start with conservative sync.
• Manual sync: user-triggered with rate limit.

Do not assume Railway free-tier services are always-on. Verify current pricing/sleep/usage limits before choosing the hosting plan. Display last successful sync and scheduler heartbeat in the UI.

