14. MVP scope and phased delivery

Phase 0 — Product validation and source feasibility (highest priority)

Deliver:

• 3–5 day validation report.
• Source matrix with official docs, terms, record types, access, fields, quotas and blockers.
• Sample opportunity dataset labelled by human.
• Manual intake prototype specification.
• Upwork and Freelancer.com feasibility decisions.
Exit:
• At least one valid path to real freelance project records (marketplace API if approved, otherwise user-assisted manual intake).
• Remote role feeds clearly separate.
• No unverified source treated as live.

Phase 1 — Data integrity and domain separation

Deliver:

• Separate freelance project and remote role domain types.
• Remove fabricated seed/live opportunities and positive trust defaults.
• Null unknown values.
• Database as sole production source of truth.
• Durable source provenance and dedup.
Exit:
• No fabricated opportunities or trust metrics.
• Repeat sync is idempotent.
• Database failure is visible.

Phase 2 — Manual intake and real source adapters

Deliver:

• Secure manual URL/text intake.
• Himalayas, Jobicy, Remote OK remote-role adapters.
• Freelancer.com adapter only if source gate passes.
• Upwork adapter only after account/API approval and scope confirmation.
Exit:
• Each active adapter has contract tests and attribution.
• Manual intake works when marketplace APIs are unavailable.

Phase 3 — Portfolio intelligence

